  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Change of use of the ground floor from Class E (Barber Shop) to a sui generis use comprising a takeaway and delivery only food premises (no primary cooking or extraction system required), operating between 10:00 and 20:00.",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-4934c5a2-7fff-a185-5f84-d7b5e199d9b8&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;Insufficient information has been provided to adequately assess or demonstrate the likely transport impacts of the use, including delivery movements and associated highway activity. As such, the proposal would result in an unknown impact on highway safety contrary to Policy LP43 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and Policy T6 of the London Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed hot food takeaway by reason of its food offer and location within a close proximity of nearby schools, would contribute to detrimental child obesity levels and health inequalities within the area, contrary to policies LP39 of the Hackney Local Plan (2020), Policy E9 of the London Plan (2021), Paragraph 96(c) of the NPPF 2024 and PPG.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
